Now, it says he buys twice as many red ties as blue ties. Since he bought 5 blue ties, the number of red ties would be twice that, so 2 times 5 equals 10. So, 10 red ties.

Next, the red ties cost 50% more than the blue ties. The blue ties are $40 each, so 50% more would be adding half of 40 to the original price. 50% of 40 is 20, so red ties cost 40 + 20 = $60 each. Alternatively, I could think of it as 1.5 times 40, which is also 60. That seems right.

So, the cost for red ties is $60 per tie. He bought 10 red ties, so total cost for red ties is 10 times 60. Let me calculate that: 10 * 60 = 600. So, he spent $600 on red ties.

